.TH mbcalibration_export 1 "8 May 2026" "MB-System 5.0" "MB-System 5.0"
.SH NAME
\fBmbcalibration_export\fP \- Export per-ping calibration data from processed swath sonar files to NetCDF4.

.SH VERSION
Version 5.0

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmbcalibration_export\fP \fB\-I\fP\fIdatalist\fP \fB\-O\fP\fIoutput.nc\fP
[\fB\-\-platform\-file=\fP\fIpath\fP]
[\fB\-\-kluge\-flipsign\-pitch\fP]
[\fB\-\-kluge\-flipsign\-roll\fP]
[\fB\-\-kluge\-soundspeed\-tweak=\fP\fIfactor\fP]
[\fB\-\-attitude\-zero\-heave\fP]
[\fB\-V\fP] [\fB\-H\fP]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmbcalibration_export\fP reads MB-System processed .mb89 files together
with their ancillary files (.fnv and .baa) produced by \fBmbpreprocess\fP,
and exports per-ping calibration data to a NetCDF4 file for use by an
automated extrinsics calibration pipeline.

The tool is designed for ROV/AUV multibeam surveys where the sonar mounting
angles (attitude offset) and position offsets relative to the navigation sensor need to
be calibrated from overlapping swath data. The exported NetCDF4 file contains
everything the optimizer needs:

.IP \(bu 2
Per-ping navigation (lon/lat/depth/heading) after position offset correction
.IP \(bu 2
Raw INS attitude (roll/pitch) from the .baa ancillary file, \fIbefore\fP
any platform attitude offset correction is applied — as required by the optimizer
.IP \(bu 2
Per-beam world-frame sounding positions (lon/lat/depth)
.IP \(bu 2
Beam quality flags
.IP \(bu 2
Starting extrinsics from the platform file,
embedded as NetCDF global attributes for use as optimizer initial conditions
.IP \(bu 2
Preprocessing flags that affected the data geometry

The ancillary files (.fnv, .baa) must be present alongside each .mb89 file.
They are produced by running \fBmbpreprocess\fP with the
\fB\-\-output\-sensor\-fnv\fP flag.

.SH MB-SYSTEM COMPATIBILITY
\fBmbcalibration_export\fP reads only processed .mb89 files and their
ancillary files. It does not modify any existing MB-System files and has
no effect on the behavior of other MB-System tools.

.SH AUTHORSHIP
Sebastian Rodriguez (srodriguez@mbari.org)
.br
Monterey Bay Aquarium Research Institute

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-H
This "help" flag causes the program to print out a description of its
operation and then exit immediately.

.TP
.B \-I \fIdatalist\fP
Sets the filename of the file containing a list of the input swath sonar
data files and their formats. In the \fBMB-System\fP datalist format, each
swath data file is followed by a data format identifier. A datalist must
contain data from a single survey (same platform file and preprocessing
parameters) because the metadata is written once per output file.

.TP
.B \-O \fIoutput.nc\fP
Sets the name of the output NetCDF4 file. The file is overwritten if it
already exists.

.TP
.B \-\-platform\-file=\fIpath\fP
Specifies the MB-System platform file (.plf) used during preprocessing.
When provided, sensor 2 extrinsics (position and attitude offsets) are read and written
as global attributes \fIsensor2_tx_extrinsics\fP,
\fIsensor2_rx_extrinsics\fP, and \fIsensor2_tx_extrinsics\fP.
These serve as the optimizer's starting point. The frame convention is
Starboard/Forward/Up (meters) for position offsets and Heading/Roll/Pitch
(degrees) for attitude offset.

.TP
.B \-\-kluge\-flipsign\-pitch
Records that \fBmbpreprocess\fP was run with \fB\-\-kluge\-flipsign\-pitch\fP,
which inverts the sign of pitch in the INS attitude stream. This is required
for INS systems (e.g., Phins C7) that report pitch with the opposite sign
convention from what MB-System expects. The flag is written as the global
attribute \fIkluge_flipsign_pitch=1\fP. Note: the pitch values in the
exported .baa-derived \fIroll_raw\fP/\fIpitch_raw\fP variables already
reflect this correction (applied during mbpreprocess); this flag is metadata
only.

.TP
.B \-\-kluge\-flipsign\-roll
Records that \fBmbpreprocess\fP was run with \fB\-\-kluge\-flipsign\-roll\fP.
Written as global attribute \fIkluge_flipsign_roll=1\fP.

.TP
.B \-\-kluge\-soundspeed\-tweak=\fIfactor\fP
Records the sound speed scaling factor used during preprocessing. The
factor is applied to beam RX angles via Snell's law during mbpreprocess,
changing computed depths (factor < 1 gives shallower depths). Written
as global attribute \fIkluge_soundspeed_tweak\fP. Default: 1.0.

.TP
.B \-\-attitude\-zero\-heave
Records that \fBmbpreprocess\fP was run with \fB\-\-attitude\-zero\-heave\fP,
which sets heave to zero in the depth calculation. Written as global
attribute \fIattitude_zero_heave=1\fP.

.TP
.B \-V
The \fB\-V\fP flag causes \fBmbcalibration_export\fP to print progress
messages to stderr.

.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
The output is a NetCDF4 file (HDF5 backend) with two dimensions:
\fIn_ping\fP (unlimited, one per survey ping) and \fImax_beam\fP
(fixed at the maximum beam count reported by the sonar format).

Per-beam variables use \fBNC_FILL_DOUBLE\fP for unused beam slots
beyond \fIn_beams[i]\fP. The \fIn_beams\fP variable tells consumers
how many beams are valid for each ping.

.SS Per-ping variables (dimension: n_ping)
.TP
\fIping_time\fP (float64)
Unix epoch seconds. Units: "seconds since 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z".

.TP
\fInav_lon\fP, \fInav_lat\fP (float64)
World-frame position of the target sensor (multibeam phase center)
after position offset correction from the navigation source. Units: degrees.

.TP
\fIsonar_depth\fP (float64)
Sensor depth below sea surface, positive down. Units: meters.

.TP
\fIaltitude\fP (float64)
Height above seafloor. Units: meters.

.TP
\fIheading\fP (float64)
True heading. Units: degrees.

.TP
\fIspeed\fP (float64)
Speed. Units: km/hr.

.TP
\fIroll_raw\fP, \fIpitch_raw\fP (float64)
Raw INS roll and pitch from the .baa ancillary file, interpolated to
ping transmit time. These are the attitude values \fIbefore\fP the
platform attitude offset rotation is applied. The optimizer applies trial
attitude offset corrections to these values. Sign convention: bow-up pitch
positive, starboard-down roll positive.

.TP
\fIheave\fP (float64)
Heave at ping time from the .fnv ancillary file. Units: meters.

.TP
\fIn_beams\fP (int32)
Number of valid beams for this ping. Beam arrays are filled up to this
index; slots beyond are fill values.

.SS Per-beam variables (dimensions: n_ping, max_beam)
.TP
\fIbath_depth\fP (float64)
Sounding depth for each beam, positive down. Units: meters.
This is the depth after all platform corrections (position offset and attitude offset)
were applied by \fBmbpreprocess\fP.

.TP
\fIbath_lon\fP, \fIbath_lat\fP (float64)
World-frame longitude and latitude of each beam sounding. Units: degrees.

.TP
\fIamplitude\fP (float32)
Beam amplitude. Units: dB (sensor-dependent).

.TP
\fIbeam_flag\fP (uint8)
Full MB-System beam quality flag. See MB-System documentation for flag
bit definitions.

.TP
\fIbeam_ok\fP (uint8)
1 if the beam is flagged as good (mb_beam_ok() is true), 0 otherwise.
Convenience variable for filtering.

.SS Global attributes
Key metadata attributes embedded in the NetCDF file:

.TP
\fImbsystem_version\fP
MB-System version string used to produce this file.

.TP
\fIcreation_time\fP
ISO-8601 UTC timestamp when the file was created.

.TP
\fIcommand_line\fP
The exact command used to run \fBmbcalibration_export\fP.

.TP
\fIplatform_file\fP
Path to the platform file, if \fB\-\-platform\-file\fP was specified.

.TP
\fIsensor2_tx_extrinsics\fP, \fIsensor2_rx_extrinsics\fP
[S, F, U] position offsets for the TX and RX arrays of sensor 2 in the
Starboard/Forward/Up frame, in meters. Populated when
\fB\-\-platform\-file\fP is provided.

.TP
\fIsensor2_tx_extrinsics\fP
[H, R, P] attitude offset of sensor 2 in Heading/Roll/Pitch degrees.
This is the starting point for the calibration optimizer.

.TP
\fIkluge_flipsign_pitch\fP, \fIkluge_flipsign_roll\fP
Integer (0 or 1). Records whether pitch or roll sign was inverted
during preprocessing.

.TP
\fIkluge_soundspeed_tweak\fP
Float. Sound speed scaling factor applied during preprocessing.

.TP
\fIattitude_zero_heave\fP
Integer (0 or 1). Records whether heave was zeroed during preprocessing.

.TP
\fIframe_convention\fP
"starboard-forward-up" — the coordinate frame for position offsets.

.TP
\fIpitch_sign_convention\fP
"bow-up-positive" — pitch is positive when the bow is elevated.

.TP
\fIroll_pitch_source\fP
"raw INS before attitude offset (from .baa ancillary file)"

.SH EXAMPLES
Export a survey with platform file and preprocessing flags:
.br
.B mbcalibration_export -I datalist.mb-1 -O cal_2025.nc \\\\
.br
.B "    " --platform-file=../platform.plf \\\\
.br
.B "    " --kluge-soundspeed-tweak=0.9996 -V

Export a Phins C7 survey (requires pitch sign correction):
.br
.B mbcalibration_export -I datalist.mb-1 -O cal_2026.nc \\\\
.br
.B "    " --platform-file=../platform.plf \\\\
.br
.B "    " --kluge-flipsign-pitch --attitude-zero-heave -V

Read the output in Python:
.nf
    import netCDF4 as nc
    import numpy as np

    ds = nc.Dataset('cal_2025.nc')

    # Starting extrinsics for the optimizer
    attitude offset = ds.getncattr('sensor2_tx_extrinsics')  # [H, R, P] deg
    tx_lever  = ds.getncattr('sensor2_tx_extrinsics')    # [S, F, U] m

    # Per-ping data
    ping_time = ds['ping_time'][:]       # Unix epoch seconds
    nav_lon   = ds['nav_lon'][:]         # degrees
    nav_lat   = ds['nav_lat'][:]         # degrees
    roll_raw  = ds['roll_raw'][:]        # degrees, before attitude offset
    pitch_raw = ds['pitch_raw'][:]       # degrees, before attitude offset

    # Per-beam world-frame soundings (good beams only)
    for i in range(len(ping_time)):
        nb = ds['n_beams'][i]
        ok = ds['beam_ok'][i, :nb] == 1
        lon   = ds['bath_lon'][i, :nb][ok]
        lat   = ds['bath_lat'][i, :nb][ok]
        depth = ds['bath_depth'][i, :nb][ok]

    ds.close()
.fi

.SH NOTES
The kluge flags passed to \fBmbcalibration_export\fP must match those used
in the \fBmbpreprocess\fP command that produced the .mb89 files. The tool
does not apply these corrections — it records them as metadata so the
calibration optimizer can correctly interpret the attitude convention.

The \fIroll_raw\fP and \fIpitch_raw\fP variables come from the .baa
ancillary file and represent the INS attitude \fIafter\fP any sign-flip
kluge applied during \fBmbpreprocess\fP, and \fIbefore\fP the platform
attitude offset rotation. The world-frame soundings (\fIbath_depth\fP,
\fIbath_lon\fP, \fIbath_lat\fP) have the current attitude offset baked in —
they represent the "ground truth" reference surface against which the
optimizer tests trial attitude offset values.

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmbsystem\fP(1), \fBmbpreprocess\fP(1), \fBmbmakeplatform\fP(1),
\fBmbinfo\fP(1), \fBmbnavlist\fP(1)

.SH BUGS
The kluge flags must be specified manually by the user — they are not
automatically read from the .par parameter file. This means the user
must ensure consistency between the mbpreprocess command and the
mbcalibration_export command.
